Q: MemberNotNull doesn&#39;t work on static instantiator A: <p>It still works, just for <code>static</code> members only.</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>public class Container {
    private static string _uniqueIdentifier; // must be initialized.

    // would get warning here if we didn't use MemberNotNull
    static Container(){
        Helper();
    }

    [MemberNotNull(nameof(_uniqueIdentifier))]
    private static void Helper() {
        _uniqueIdentifier = DateTime.Now.Ticks.ToString();
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>To me it's logical or at least consistent that instance helper methods are responsible for instance members and static helper methods for static members.</p>

Q: Jest: &quot;Directory in the roots[0] option was not found&quot; A: <p>For me the following code in config-overrides.js worked.</p>
<pre><code>module.exports = {
  jest: function(config) {
    config.collectCoverageFrom = ['client/**/*.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}', '!client/**/*.d.ts'];
    config.testMatch = [
      '&lt;rootDir&gt;/client/**/__tests__/**/*.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}',
      '&lt;rootDir&gt;/client/**/*.{spec,test}.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}',
    ];
    config.roots = ['&lt;rootDir&gt;/client'];
    return config;
  },

  // The paths config
  paths: function(paths, env) {
    paths.appIndexJs = path.resolve(__dirname, 'client/index.js');
    paths.appSrc = path.resolve(__dirname, 'client');
    return paths;
  },
};
</code></pre>
<p>I have renamed my src folder created by cra to client and added the path config part to reflect that. That on its own isn't enough, hence the jest part. Just config your paths to reflect your own structure.</p>
